				923,
				8
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Modularize IPC and RPC layers into PascalCase submodules\n\nDecompose the monolithic IPC and RPC documentation files and inline re-exports into dedicated submodule trees to align with the project-wide PascalCase naming convention.\n\nFor the IPC layer, remove extensive inline documentation and `pub use` re-exports from `Common`, `Connection`, `Message`, and `IPC` root modules. Extract types into explicit submodules (`ConnectionStatus`, `Health`, `Types`, `Manager`) and enforce callers to use full paths (e.g., `IPC::Message::Types::TauriIPCMessage`). Update `Source/ExtensionManagement/Scanner.rs` and `Source/IPC/Encryption/` imports to reflect the new `Utility::ErrorMapping` and `Message::Types` paths.\n\nFor the RPC layer, strip the 100+ line architectural documentation and feature-gate re-exports from `Source/RPC/mod.rs`. Retain only the active `CocoonService` implementation as the primary surface, while preserving `EchoAction`, `Commands`, `Workspace`, and other service modules as scaffolding for the multi-extension-host roadmap.\n\nThis structural refactor eliminates implicit imports, enforces strict PascalCase function and type naming across the IPC/RPC stack, and establishes a consistent, atomic namespace hierarchy for future expansion of the Spine contract.",
			"SHA": "df5e882e611928e12ddbcc010fc00df57017e31c"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-02T01:13:56Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				923,
				31
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Modularize Utility error mapping and security into PascalCase submodules\n\nDecompose the monolithic `Utility` module in the Environment provider by removing public re-exports that violated the project-wide PascalCase naming convention. Extract logical units into dedicated submodules: `ErrorMapping` for `MapApplicationStateLockErrorToCommonError` and `UriParsing` for URI-to-URL conversion logic, while consolidating path validation into `PathSecurity`.\n\nUpdate all 26+ Environment provider implementations (Command, Configuration, Diagnostic, Document, FileSystem, and others) to call these utilities via their explicit full paths (`Utility::ErrorMapping::Fn`, `Utility::UriParsing::Fn`, `Utility::PathSecurity::Fn`) rather than through the flat namespace. This structural refactor eliminates implicit imports, enforces strict PascalCase function naming across the codebase, and establishes a consistent, atomic namespace hierarchy for future utility expansion.",
			"SHA": "b72100dc594a09915d480112e7d77972a5b18794"
		}
	],
